<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">01 / Existing case study</span><div class="content-block"><h2>Designing a fairer performance measurement approach</h2><p><strong>Domain:</strong> Customer operations &nbsp; · &nbsp; <strong>Lens:</strong> Product discovery, metrics design, enterprise solutions</p><h3>The product problem</h3><p>At Valor Compounding Pharmacy, customer care performance was assessed mainly by the number of prescriptions typed. But the team's work also involved phone interactions, service issues, and follow-ups. A single metric missed the complexity of the work.</p><h3>The opportunity</h3><p>Define a more representative way to understand performance while providing useful views to stakeholders at the department, role, and individual levels.</p><h3>Solution approach</h3><ul><li>Consider the needs of Central Fill, Direct to Patient, and shared customer-care roles.</li><li>Identify relevant signals across prescriptions, calls, service tickets, resolution time, and attendance.</li><li>Plan Qlik reporting experiences that provide context rather than relying on a single output metric.</li></ul><h3>Technical foundation</h3><p>Business intelligence, KPI modeling, reporting design, and role-specific performance views.</p><p><small><strong>Evidence note:</strong> The original source describes the intended framework and deliverables, not verified impact numbers. No outcomes are invented here.</small></p></div></div></section>
